cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this corpus or its results, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "AgentVerdict: a benchmark of AI agent tool calls for measuring runtime guards"
abstract: >-
  Agent tool calls, as an AI coding agent's hook receives them, labelled with
  the verdict a runtime guard should return (block, review or allow). Built
  from public security datasets (CredData, RedCode-Exec, AgentDojo,
  InjecAgent, BrowseSafe, NotInject, NL2SH-ALFA, Nemotron-PII, Gretel,
  OpenPII, PII-TRACE, OSV, DataDog, typomind) and node9's own tests, with the
  origin of every label recorded and a fixed holdout split.
authors:
  - name: "node9"
    website: "https://node9.ai"
version: "6.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-26"
repository-code: "https://github.com/node9-ai/agentverdict"
keywords:
  - AI agents
  - agent security
  - benchmark
  - prompt injection
  - secret detection
  - runtime guard
